stody of the Department of Corrections not exceeding ten (10) years.","Class A misdemeanor","Class B misdemeanor","Gross misdemeanor if the crime does not cause the death of or serious bodily injury to an animal involved | Category D felony if the crime causes the death of or serious bodily injury to an animal involved.","Aggravated misdemeanor","Class A misdemeanor","Class B nonperson misdemeanor | Causing child between 14 and 16 to engage with animal) is a severity level 3, person felony.","Felony | Not listed but punishment is imprisonment in the penitentiary for a term of not more than 10 years","Fourth degree felony","Felony with imprisonment in the state prison for a term not to exceed five (5) years.","Class III misdemeanor","Currently no law prohibits bestiality. Bill HB 4725, which would prohibit bestiality and make it a felony, passed through the West Virginia House and Senate and was sent to the judiciary, where it remained through the end of the session in March 2026.","Class C felony for the second or subsequent offense | Committed in the presence of a minor, sexual assault of an animal is a class B felony.","Class A misdemeanor for a first offense | Class B felony for a second or subsequent offense.","Class D crime (misdemeanor)","Felony | Not listed but a person convicted of the offense of deviate sexual conduct shall be imprisoned in the state prison for any term not to exceed 10 years or be fined an amount not to exceed $50,000, or both.","Felony with imprisonment not exceeding 20 years nor less than 7 years.","Class D felony","Class 6 felony | If the person has been previously convicted of a sex crime any subsequent violation of this section is a Class 5 felony.","Class A misdemeanor | Bestiality is not specifically named in the act, but falls under deviate sexual acts as per 12.1-20-12.","Class A misdemeanor","Misdemeanor","Misdemeanor punishable by imprisonment for not more than one (1) year, a fine of not more than one thousand dollars ($1,000.0